# Ball_Basic - the cue ball: warm white, cool shadows, the blue paw print as a decal.
# Reference painting for the kit: draft the ball, bucket-fill it, shade the form, then paint the decal on top.
# Ball family (all Ball_*.paint): one circle (ellipse K 16 16 14.8 14.8), light from the top-left, a shadow
# crescent (band 7), a core shadow (band 3), a 1 px reflected light on the bottom-right rim (band 1), one
# highlight streak, the outline lightened where it faces the light. Emblems are decals without an outline:
# lit colour where the ball is lit, the decal's shade colour where it crosses the shadow crescent.
size 32 32
key
  K #2b2e40  ink (outer line)
  k #4d536c  outline on the lit side
  W #e9ebf1  ball base
  s #c3c8d8  shadow / reflected light
  S #9097b2  core shadow
  H #ffffff  highlight
  B #5b78bb  paw
  b #3b5192  paw shade (edge and inside the shadow crescent)
strokes
  ellipse K 16 16 14.8 14.8
seeds
  W 16 16
ops
  band W s 1 1 7
  band W S 1 1 3
  band W s 1 1 1
# the paw: four toe beans and the palm pad; the right toe and the palm's right side sit in the crescent
shade at 8 9
  ....BB....BB....
  ...BBBB..BBBB...
  ...BBBb..BBBb...
  ....bb....bb....
  .BB..........Bb.
  BBBB........BBbb
  BBBb..BBBB..Bbbb
  .bb.BBBBBBBB.bb.
  ...BBBBBBBBBb...
  ..BBBBBBBBBbbb..
  ..BBBBBBBBbbbb..
  ..BBBBBBBbbbbb..
  ...bbbb..bbbb...
# highlight: one window streak following the top-left rim
shade at 6 5
  ....HH
  ..HHHH
  .HHHH.
  .HH...
ops
  edge K k -1 -1
  px k 2 19 19 2
  px K 3 23 23 3
